WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.520
Ancient Greece.

2
00:00:01.570 --> 00:00:05.590
An open-air theatre, and
a masked actor steps out.

3
00:00:05.640 --> 00:00:08.650
Centuries later, a crowded playhouse.

4
00:00:08.700 --> 00:00:12.220
People pay at the door to
watch a great man fall.

5
00:00:12.270 --> 00:00:17.680
At the end, a general asks to be
remembered as "one that loved not wisely,

6
00:00:17.730 --> 00:00:19.130
but too well".

7
00:00:19.180 --> 00:00:20.570
They knew the ending.

8
00:00:20.620 --> 00:00:22.150
They paid anyway.

9
00:00:22.200 --> 00:00:25.020
So why watch a good person destroyed?

10
00:00:25.070 --> 00:00:29.270
In this mission, you'll meet the first
theory of tragedy ever written down, by

11
00:00:29.320 --> 00:00:30.480
Aristotle.

12
00:00:30.530 --> 00:00:34.150
You'll ask what kind of person
a tragic hero has to be.

13
00:00:34.200 --> 00:00:34.960
A villain?

14
00:00:35.010 --> 00:00:35.990
A saint?

15
00:00:36.040 --> 00:00:39.440
And you'll meet one Greek word, catharsis.

16
00:00:39.490 --> 00:00:44.460
Your mission: explain why audiences
pay to watch a good person destroyed.
